# No per-skin engine hacks

The skin runtime (`src/lib/skin*.ts`, `src/components/playback/skin/`), WMS importer, and `spk-format` schemas are a **general engine**. A bug in one pack is a missing pattern in the engine or missing data on the presentation — not an `if` for that pack.

## Do not

- Fingerprint a skin, pack, or view (`id === "lost-planet"`, inset tuples that only that pack uses, asset filenames as identity)
- Hardcode radii, z-index, or layout that only one skin’s art happens to need
- Add “just this pack” branches, feature flags, or special-case helpers named after a skin

```ts
// ❌ BAD — engine knows a product
function isLostPlanetClientHole(inset: TiledFrameContentInset): boolean {
  return inset.left === 16 && inset.top === 42 && …;
}

// ✅ GOOD — pack authors the pattern; engine reads it
tiledFrameContentRadius(presentation) // presentation.contentCornerRadius ?? 0
```

## Do

- Encode the **WMS/Spiral pattern** (overlay glaze vs corner cap, client-hole clip, stretch tiles)
- Put skin-specific numbers on the **manifest / assets** (`contentCornerRadius`, masks, tiles)
- Use pack names in **tests and comments as examples** of a general rule, not as runtime identity

If a second skin would need the same `if`, the condition was never a skin check — lift it into the format.
